{title: His Steadfast Love Endures Forever}
{subtitle: Psalm 136}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Give thanks to the LORD, for he is good
His steadfast [Eb/G]love endures [Ab]for[Bb7sus4]ev[Eb]er
Give thanks to the God of gods
His [Ab]steadfast love en[Bb]dures forev[Eb]er
Give thanks to the Lord of lords
His [Ab]steadfast love en[Bb]dures forev[Eb]er
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
To him who alone does great wonders
His [Ab]steadfast love en[Bb]dures forev[Eb]er
To him who made the heavens with understanding
His [Ab]steadfast love en[Bb]dures forev[Eb]er
To him who spread out the earth upon the waters
His [Ab]steadfast love en[Bb]dures forev[Eb]er
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
To him who made the great lights
His [Ab]steadfast love en[Bb]dures forev[Eb]er
The sun to rule over the day
His [Ab]steadfast love en[Bb]dures forev[Eb]er
The moon and stars to rule over the night
His [Ab]steadfast love en[Bb]dures forev[Eb]er
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Who remembered us when we were brought low
His [Ab]steadfast love en[Bb]dures forev[Eb]er
And broke us free from our foes
His [Ab]steadfast love en[Bb]dures forev[Eb]er
Who gives food to all flesh
His [Ab]steadfast love en[Bb]dures forev[Eb]er
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Give thanks to the God of heaven
His [Abmaj7]steadfast love en[Bb]dures forev[Eb]er
His [Abmaj7]steadfast love en[Bb]dures forev[Eb]er
{end_of_verse}
